WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.540
It's a new day in Wakanda, with a new face
on the throne, a new Black Panther, and a

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.700
fearsome ocean-dwelling new enemy.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.679
There's even a new "Iron" person – and plenty
of questions about what's coming next.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.700
Warning: major spoilers ahead for "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:00:17.251 --> 00:00:22.870
After King T'Chaka meets his untimely end
in "Captain America: Civil War," his son T'Challa

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.189
becomes the new leader of Wakanda.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:31.109
In order to make his position official, T'Challa
goes through a ceremony involving ritual combat.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:35.899
But when T'Challa himself dies before the
events of "Wakanda Forever," Ramonda becomes

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:38.829
the country's leader, apparently by default.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:43.930
Shuri, the only other royal in Wakanda, seems
fine with this situation, as she prefers to

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.770
spend her time in her lab.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:52.170
But then Ramonda abruptly dies due to Namor's
actions, making Shuri Wakanda's de facto leader.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.930
This development is overshadowed by the fact
that Shuri also becomes the Black Panther

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.160
shortly afterward.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.877
It's this superheroic title she invokes to
declare war on Namor and his people.

00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:05.467
"Without the Black Panther…Wakanda will
fall."

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:09.990
In one of the final scenes of "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever," the ceremony that solidified

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:14.950
T'Challa's leadership is staged once more,
indicating that Shuri is ready to officially

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.250
become queen.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.970
But it's M'Baku, not Shuri, who emerges to
take part in the ritual.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.710
Fans know that M'Baku has coveted the throne
since the first "Black Panther" film, in which

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.250
he challenges T'Challa and loses.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.540
But in this case, there's no one there to
challenge.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.890
Does that mean M'Baku gets the throne by default?

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:37.710
While Shuri deliberately skips the ceremony,
it's not clear if she sent M'Baku in her place

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.770
with the intention of making him king.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:40.899
It's certainly possible.

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:45.370
Shuri's never seemed all that interested in
leadership, and she might feel that M'Baku

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.920
is a better choice for the role.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.290
But ultimately, the question of who will be
the country's new leader is left open.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:56.810
One of the biggest developments in "Black
Panther: Wakanda Forever" is the introduction

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.830
of Riri Williams, a genius MIT student and
the inventor of the vibranium detection device

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.630
that the United States uses to search for
the valuable metal.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.950
This invention puts her squarely in Namor's
crosshairs.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:14.970
Shuri and Okoye travel to America to protect
Riri, and soon learn she's created an Iron

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.340
Man-style suit in her garage.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.670
When she joins the fight against Namor and
the Talokans, it's mainly to repay her debt

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.910
to Wakanda for saving her.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.500
Being a superhero long-term doesn't seem to
be part of Riri's plans, and by the end of

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.470
the movie, she's on her way back to MIT.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.830
This surely isn't the last we'll see of her,
though.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:38.640
For one thing, she's the star of the upcoming
"Ironheart" Disney+ series, which indicates

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.720
she'll take up the call of a hero and become
an official do-gooder.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.640
Plus, she's one of many young superheroes
introduced in the Marvel Cinematic Universe's

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.940
Phase 4, including America Chavez, Ms. Marvel,
and Kate Bishop.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.340
Riri seems all but certain to team up with
them as part of a Young Avengers-style group

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.665
somewhere down the line.

00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:03.330
Okoye has a life-altering storyline in "Black
Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.970
Not only is she devastated by T'Challa's death,
but a frantic Ramonda, who blames her for

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.409
losing Shuri to Namor and the Talokans in
Boston, fires her from the Dora Milaje.

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:16.920
And it seems like Okoye does her best to leave
her former life behind.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.750
When Ramonda dies and Shuri comes to enlist
her in the fight against the Talokans, Okoye

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.560
initially seems reluctant.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:29.519
Fortunately, Shuri has an added incentive:
a suit she refers to as the Midnight Angel.

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:34.239
Throughout the film, Shuri tries to get Okoye
to accept upgrades to the Dora Milaje's armor

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:36.780
and weapons, with no real luck.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.590
But things change when Okoye sees Shuri's
Midnight Angel prototype.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:46.560
She, along with Ayo and Aneka, wear the new
suits during the movie's climactic final battle.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.060
Not only does this allow Okoye to jump back
into action, it also means she's part of a

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.209
new elite fighting unit.

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:58.129
Comic book fans will recognize the Midnight
Angels as a strike force within the Dora Milaje.

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:03.966
In their very first outing, they take on the
infamous Dr. Doom after he steals Wakanda's vibranium.

00:04:03.966 --> 00:04:07.780
Could this mean that Okoye and the Midnight
Angels will be the vehicle through which the

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.120
Fantastic Four antagonist is introduced to
the MCU?

00:04:11.388 --> 00:04:12.388
Possibly.

00:04:12.388 --> 00:04:14.099
Here's what we do know.

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:18.880
The last we see of Okoye in "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever," she's rescuing Agent Everett

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.370
Ross from CIA custody entirely solo, likely
at Shuri's request.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:29.300
One way or another, Okoye is once again an
important player in Wakanda's affairs, and

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.358
could become a more visible figure in the
larger MCU.

00:04:33.438 --> 00:04:37.540
In "Black Panther," Killmonger burns all of
the heart-shaped herbs that empower the Black

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.259
Panther, in an effort to prevent anyone else
from gaining its impressive gifts.

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:47.130
Shuri spends most of "Wakanda Forever" attempting
to genetically engineer a new version of the

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:50.100
herb, and endures repeated failures.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.039
But then, she uses a leaf that is part of
a gift from Namor, which turns out to have

00:04:54.039 --> 00:04:56.520
similar properties as the heart-shaped herb.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.370
Shuri discovers how to reconstitute the herb,
thanks to this addition, and hastily ingests

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.030
it, making her the new Black Panther.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:08.980
By the end of the film, Wakandans are planting
the newly reborn heart-shaped herb, ensuring

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.880
they have a supply for future Wakandan protectors.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:17.442
In many ways, Shuri's decision to become the
Black Panther makes sense, based on Wakanda's history.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:21.740
She's the nation's current leader, and the
leader and Black Panther are often the same

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.720
person, though this is not necessarily a requirement.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.582
Plus, Shuri has repeatedly proven herself
a capable fighter when the need arises.

00:05:29.582 --> 00:05:33.468
"Only the most broken people...can be great
leaders."

00:05:33.468 --> 00:05:38.500
However, by the end of the film, her desire
to stay on the Wakandan throne is in question.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.160
Shuri's greatest skill remains her scientific
genius, and the stunning technological advances

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.090
it enables her to create.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.840
It's possible that Shuri could abdicate her
responsibility as the leader of Wakanda, or

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.030
at least share the duties with another.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.190
Maybe the role of the ruler and Black Panther
could split, allowing the latter to focus

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.389
on the day-to-day protection of the nation.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:01.720
If M'baku becomes king, would he allow such
an arrangement?

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:08.360
CIA agent Everett Ross is drawn into the plot
of "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" when Okoye

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.740
and Shuri travel to America and approach him
for the name of the individual who created

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.020
the vibranium-detecting device.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.670
While Ross is reluctant to share the information,
he eventually relents, because of his ongoing

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.380
loyalty to the Wakandans.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.039
By giving up the name, he commits a crime
against the United States.

00:06:25.039 --> 00:06:29.250
Unfortunately for him, it's only a matter
of time before the CIA director discovers

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.610
his treachery.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:35.199
The fact that the CIA director happens to
be Valentina Allegra de Fontaine, the woman

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:40.090
who's been pulling strings behind the scenes
with people like John Walker, aka U.S. Agent,

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:44.270
and Yelena Belova — not to mention the shocking
revelation that she used to be married to

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.760
Agent Ross — brings up all sorts of questions
about what Val's endgame is and how Ross could

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.190
play a part in it.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:55.379
Val's decision to have Ross arrested and taken
into custody is actually pretty by-the-books,

00:06:55.379 --> 00:06:56.590
given what he does.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:00.479
Whether she feels this gives her an advantage
in her shadowy plans or she just wants to

00:07:00.479 --> 00:07:05.490
make Ross pay for sharing American secrets
because she's a good CIA director isn't clear.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:10.310
Either way, with Ross now free and likely
in Wakanda after being rescued by Okoye, it's

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:14.669
natural to wonder if this could set up a showdown
between Val and the Wakandans.

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:18.880
Ross doesn't seem to especially like Val,
but there is a certain familiarity there that

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.467
could be useful, if and when she stirs up
trouble in the future.

00:07:22.591 --> 00:07:27.790
That could happen in the upcoming "Thunderbolts"
movie, or another production altogether.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.259
The introduction of Namor is a big deal for
both the world of the "Black Panther" movies

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:37.530
and the MCU as a whole, especially since he's
the rare Marvel antagonist who survives the

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.389
conclusion of the film.

00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:43.610
In the end, he ends up agreeing to a truce
between Wakanda and Talokan, bringing the

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.949
fight between the two countries to an end.

00:07:45.949 --> 00:07:50.449
However, the Talokans are incredibly antagonistic
to Wakanda and the rest of the world throughout

00:07:50.449 --> 00:07:51.449
the film.

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:56.430
They first kill everyone in the American research
facility searching for vibranium in the ocean

00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:02.780
depths, and later attack Wakanda after Nakia
kills a Talokan while rescuing Shuri and Riri.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:06.490
Throughout the movie, Namor rails against
the evils of the surface world.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:10.580
He wants to keep Talokan hidden from those
who dwell on land, and seems prepared to kill

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.860
anyone who could compromise that objective.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:17.639
It seems his people agree with this stance,
to the point that the truce with Wakanda frustrates

00:08:17.639 --> 00:08:18.680
at least some of them.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:24.139
Yet, when Namora confronts him about his decision
to walk away peacefully, Namor ominously claims

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:28.509
that when the surface world comes for Wakanda,
Wakanda will turn to Talokan.

00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:33.300
Namor seems to think that Wakanda's resources
will be too much for the world to resist,

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.920
eventually leading to a massive war only the
Talokans can help them fight.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:40.740
At that point, the Talokans will have the
opportunity to bring the surface world to

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.390
its knees, as they originally planned.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:48.279
However, it's hard to imagine the whole world
openly taking on Wakanda, or that Wakanda

00:08:48.279 --> 00:08:52.110
would need Talokan's help against far less
technologically advanced countries.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:57.080
On the other hand, it's undeniable that the
world is preoccupied with finding vibranium.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.360
Namor might very well have a point.

00:09:00.746 --> 00:09:05.620
Fans who are eagerly awaiting the appearance
of the X-Men in the MCU are likely to cheer

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:10.440
when Namor refers to himself as a mutant in
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:15.380
The comics often describe him as the first
mutant, so his emergence as the MCU's first

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.959
official member of that group creates a wonderful
symmetry.

00:09:18.959 --> 00:09:23.560
While there have been hints about the existence
of mutants in the MCU before, most prominently

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.850
in the Disney+ series "Ms. Marvel…"

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:31.470
"Kamala, there's something different in your
genes.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.756
Like, like a mutation."

00:09:34.004 --> 00:09:37.250
…Namor is the first to identify himself
this way.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:41.440
Moreover, based on the origins he shares with
his underwater kingdom, he's been around for

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.930
a very long time.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:47.540
Namor's introduction suggests there could
be many other mutants in the MCU just waiting

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.540
to be revealed.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:53.300
No plans have yet been announced for an official
MCU "X-Men" film, but we know Logan will be

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.149
part of "Deadpool 3."

00:09:55.149 --> 00:09:56.279
What could this mean?

00:09:56.279 --> 00:10:01.040
Just like the MCU has introduced several possible
members of a Young Avengers-style super-team,

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.570
so too could the MCU introduce mutant characters
with the goal of bringing them together in

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.100
an X-Men-esque group.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.790
Namor could also play an important role in
a variety of other outings, including the

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:14.580
MCU's upcoming "Fantastic Four" film.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:20.910
The mid-credits scene of "Black Panther: Wakanda
Forever" introduces the character of Toussaint,

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:25.390
son of Nakia and T'Challa, who reveals his
real name is T'Challa Jr.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:29.860
Nakia has kept her child a secret from the
Wakandan people at T'Challa's request.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:34.541
However, if the country's line of succession
runs through the king, then T'Challa Jr. is

00:10:34.541 --> 00:10:36.639
the rightful heir to the throne.

00:10:36.639 --> 00:10:39.700
Shuri seems surprised, but happy to meet her
nephew.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.139
It's possible her reaction is the result of
relief that there is someone else who could

00:10:43.139 --> 00:10:45.290
ultimately be responsible for leading Wakanda.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:51.070
Obviously, T'Challa Jr. is far too young to
take on the duties of a king, but either Shuri

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:55.250
or Nakia could act as his regent until he's
ready to fulfill his role.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:59.560
Moreover, T'Challa Jr. could also become the
Black Panther when he's old enough.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.570
While Nakia seems to want to keep her son
in Haiti for the time being, she indicates

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:06.519
her plan is to bring him to Wakanda eventually.

00:11:06.519 --> 00:11:08.879
The question is, when will that happen?

00:11:08.879 --> 00:11:13.620
Even more pressingly, what will it mean for
the future of Wakanda and the MCU as a whole?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.120
It's possible we won't hear about T'Challa
Jr. again for quite some time.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:22.000
At that far-off point, T'Challa Jr. could
become the leader his father intended to become

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.100
before his untimely death.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.220
But the young boy also has the potential to
cause an enormous shake-up in the Wakandan

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.329
power structure.

00:11:29.329 --> 00:11:33.889
The MCU tends to be pretty calculated in its
revelations, so we're betting that we'll see

00:11:33.889 --> 00:11:37.160
more of T'Challa Jr. sooner rather than later.

